WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.582
This final example puts the main modeling steps into one sequence.

00:00:04.582 --> 00:00:10.237
A synthetic dataset is created, then split into training and test sets.

00:00:10.237 --> 00:00:15.832
A decision tree with maximum depth three is fitted on the training data.

00:00:15.832 --> 00:00:20.723
Predictions are generated for the test set, and accuracy is calculated.

00:00:21.249 --> 00:00:28.021
The exact accuracy is less important than the workflow: data, split, train, predict, evaluate.

00:00:28.021 --> 00:00:33.781
Change the tree depth or the random state and compare what happens.

00:00:33.781 --> 00:00:40.539
Small modeling decisions can change performance, which is why reproducibility and evaluation matter.
